# Local media pilot: results and rollout proposal

Brightwell Pet Supply, field marketing. Draft for the commercial board, October 2026.

## What we did

From 6 July to 4 October 2026 (Q3) we ran outdoor posters near stores plus local radio in five regions: Bexwell, Glenhaven, Redfern, Stonebridge, Harrowgate Downs. We chose them because they had the weakest growth of all 18 regions in Q2 (Q2 vs Q1 like-for-like sales), so they had the most to gain. Cost: EUR 55,000 per region for the quarter, EUR 275,000 in total.

## Sales

| | Q2 like-for-like sales | Q3 like-for-like sales | Growth |
|---|---|---|---|
| Pilot regions | EUR 5,908,634 | EUR 6,573,336 | 11.2% |
| Company total | EUR 25,666,131 | EUR 25,620,475 | -0.2% |

The pilot regions grew **11.4 points faster** than the company. On the pilot regions' Q2 base that is about **EUR 675,213 of extra sales**, a return of **2.5x** on the EUR 275,000 spend.

The national Pet Week promotion (week of 31 August) lifted sales everywhere that week; it is in both rows above.

## Brand awareness

Aided awareness in the pilot regions rose from 31% to 44% (survey_waves.csv).

## Proposal

Roll the local media programme out to all 18 regions from Q1 2027: EUR 3,960,000 a year.
